note This file demonstrates every place where punctuation-free syntax could be
note ambiguous, and how the Clause Signature Registry resolves each one.
note Everything here parses with the reference front end:
note   python reference/shark_ref.py examples/ambiguity.shark --emit ast
note   python reference/shark_ref.py --why examples/ambiguity.shark:18

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 1. greedy text

page Home
  show text Welcome to my app, 100% of the time

page Manual
  show text The manual

page Game Over
  show text Better luck next time

note `to` alone is not a terminator phrase. `to page` is. So this label keeps
note its middle words and the button has no target.
show button Go to Top

note Here `to page` appears as a complete phrase, so the label stops at `Go`.
show button Go to page Home

note When you genuinely need a terminator phrase inside a label, use the
note explicit hanging form. This is the Sugar Law from spec/00 section 0.3.
show button
  label
    Go to page 2 of the manual
  to page
    Manual

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 2. open slots

note `show text` has an open slot, so nothing can truncate it. Commas, percent
note signs, braces and the word `to` are all just text.
show text Press {Start} to begin, or wait 10 seconds

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 3. names with spaces

note Names are matched longest first, so `Game Over` is one name, not two.
show button Give up to page Game Over

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 4. splices

keep score as 1250

show text Your score is value of score
show text Your score is value of score and rising

note To show the literal words `value of`, use a text block.
show text
  text
    The words value of are shown literally here.

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 5. numbers in text

note A number inside a text slot contributes its source spelling, not its value.
show text You have 1,000 points

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 6. word operators

keep a as 2
keep b as 3
keep c as 4

note Precedence follows arithmetic convention, so this is a plus (b times c).
let total be a plus b times c

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 7. the flush form

note A `when` body may be a single statement at the same indentation. This is
note exactly one statement, never two.
when Give up is pressed
open page Game Over

note The same thing written the way `compose format` will rewrite it.
when Give up is pressed
  open page Game Over

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 8. what is rejected

note Each of the following would be an error. They are kept as notes so this
note file still compiles.
note
note   to show a chart of a kind with some data
note     E-0312  `show` would collide with `show text`, whose first slot is
note             free text and could absorb the word `chart`.
note             Fix: `to draw a chart of a kind with some data`
note
note   page open
note     E-0342  `open` begins the phrase `open page` and cannot be a name.
note
note   page Home{2}
note     E-0101  a brace is not a name character. It is fine inside text.
note
note   show button
note     E-0231  the label slot is empty and no indented block follows.
note
note   let x be 1 is less than 2 is less than 3
note     E-0252  comparison does not chain. Write
note             `1 is less than 2 and 2 is less than 3`.

note ---------------------------------------------------------- 9. beyond the reference

note These parse under the full grammar (spec/02) but are not implemented by
note the single file reference front end, which stops at SIR-D:
note
note   set total to
note     group
note       base plus bonus
note     times multiplier
note
note   for each p in sparks at the same time
note     set life of p to life of p minus 0.016
